WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.211
A remote problem.

00:00:01.256 --> 00:00:02.226
Your AI agent.

00:00:02.272 --> 00:00:04.900
A clear path from diagnosis to resolution.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.101
The user starts Diagnose and shares a short-lived pairing code privately.

00:00:09.146 --> 00:00:11.900
Our guide explains how to install Node first.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.681
Launch Codex, Claude Code, or Gemini with Diagnose.

00:00:15.726 --> 00:00:18.900
Remote tools load for this session, without permanent setup.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.121
The user confirms the connection locally.

00:00:21.166 --> 00:00:25.900
Review each task, or explicitly allow automatic execution and transmission for this session.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.722
Commands and results are encrypted between the endpoints.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.414
The relay sees connection metadata.

00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:32.900
Your chosen AI provider can see the results.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.833
The agent collects evidence and finds a port mismatch.

00:00:35.878 --> 00:00:40.900
It explains the proposed configuration change, its impact, and how to restore the original.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.548
With permission, the agent applies the fix.

00:00:43.593 --> 00:00:47.900
Terminals, files, networks, and device tools support deeper work.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.893
Repeat the failing check, then summarize the result.

00:00:50.938 --> 00:00:54.900
Local audit events record actions, changes, and data transfers.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.320
The user can revoke access anytime.

00:00:57.365 --> 00:00:59.900
Diagnose and fix, with your AI agent.
